    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_84473009",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a person in a yellow hazmat suit spraying a field, with overlaid text reading \"once we are done destroying our country we'll move to yours!\". The scene uses a visual metaphor of environmental or agricultural destruction (spraying crops) to symbolize the act of 'destroying' a nation. The intent is to convey a message of hostility, aggression, and potential displacement or invasion, framed as a threat against another country or community. This meme is harmful because it promotes xenophobic and aggressive sentiments, suggesting that one group will abandon their own country to harm another, which can incite fear, division, and hostility between nations or communities. The overall intent is propagandistic, aiming to provoke negative emotions and reinforce a narrative of external threat or impending conflict, potentially encouraging harmful attitudes or actions toward other nations or groups.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_49e8cd6e"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
